  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Health Organization (WHO) Framework Convention on Tobacco Control 2030 (FCTC 2030) - Strengthening tobacco control in low- and middle-income countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is an Official Development Assistance (ODA) funded UKaid project from the Department of Health and Social Care (DHSC). It provides funding to the World Health Organization (WHO) for the Framework Convention on Tobacco Control (FCTC) 2030 project to promote implementation of the WHO FCTC in low- and middle-income countries (LMICs), to reduce global tobacco consumption and support the development of ODA recipient countries. The project will support LMICs to strengthen tobacco control by: (1) Implementing the requirements of Article 5 (general obligations) of the WHO FCTC, to improve tobacco control governance; (2) Increasing tobacco tax; (3) Implementing the two WHO FCTC time-bound measures on (i) tobacco packaging and (ii) ending tobacco advertising); and (4) Implementing other Articles of the WHO FCTC according to national priorities. This project was not put out to an open, competitive tender process because the UK has committed to supporting the WHO Framework Convention on Tobacco Control, a treaty adopted by the World Health Assembly in 2003. This project is led by WHO and therefore the UK provides a contribution, as there is no other project of its kind in the world.</narrative>
  </description>
